{"assets":["/statement-assets/e9282eb4afe0cf9e9e6892545e14c86fe3abbfb5b943c430fb53ba382a6825ce.png","/statement-assets/8a1d3882df812a468fec84cf6d3d55c4bf61a6bcfa60ebdb92a269657897c3fb.png","/statement-assets/18a97efb5105c15a703cb9ab36f17a18b39bc6ac658750e2da7f990cce233e3f.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"780","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Andryusha and Colored Balloons"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Andryusha goes through a park each day. The squares and paths between them look boring to Andryusha, so he decided to decorate them."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The park consists of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" squares connected with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(n - 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" bidirectional paths in such a way that any square is reachable from any other using these paths. Andryusha decided to hang a colored balloon at each of the squares. The baloons' colors are described by positive integers, starting from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":". In order to make the park varicolored, Andryusha wants to choose the colors in a special way. More precisely, he wants to use such colors that if "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c"},{"kind":"text","text":" are distinct squares that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" have a direct path between them, and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c"},{"kind":"text","text":" have a direct path between them, then balloon colors on these three squares are distinct."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Andryusha wants to use as little different colors as possible. Help him to choose the colors!"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3 ≤ n ≤ 2·105"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of squares in the park."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(n - 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ x, y ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the indices of two squares directly connected by a path."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that any square is reachable from any other using the paths."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first line print single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the minimum number of colors Andryusha has to use."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second line print "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers, the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th of them should be equal to the balloon color on the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th square. Each of these numbers should be within range from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n2 3\n1 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n1 3 2 "}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\n2 3\n5 3\n4 3\n1 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\n1 3 2 5 4 "}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\n2 1\n3 2\n4 3\n5 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n1 2 3 1 2 "}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample the park consists of three squares: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 → 3 → 2"},{"kind":"text","text":". Thus, the balloon colors have to be distinct."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/e9282eb4afe0cf9e9e6892545e14c86fe3abbfb5b943c430fb53ba382a6825ce.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Illustration for the first sample."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example there are following triples of consequently connected squares: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 → 3 → 2"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 → 3 → 4"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 → 3 → 5"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 → 3 → 4"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 → 3 → 5"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4 → 3 → 5"}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" We can see that each pair of squares is encountered in some triple, so all colors have to be distinct."},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/8a1d3882df812a468fec84cf6d3d55c4bf61a6bcfa60ebdb92a269657897c3fb.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Illustration for the second sample."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third example there are following triples: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 → 2 → 3"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 → 3 → 4"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3 → 4 → 5"}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" We can see that one or two colors is not enough, but there is an answer that uses three colors only."},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/18a97efb5105c15a703cb9ab36f17a18b39bc6ac658750e2da7f990cce233e3f.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Illustration for the third sample."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"780C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/780/problem/C"}